A still moment — no weather, no tide, no wind, nothing moving anywhere. The world holding its breath. It does this, rarely, and no one knows for what.
[Across the fringe, vast and unhurried, a Greenwatcher passes — and stops. It looks at you. It has never needed to look at anyone.]
The creature can feel which one you are long before the grid finishes deciding. Raise a thing in mercy and it grows up expecting the world to be survivable; raise it in altar-smoke and it grows up expecting to be spent. It reads tamers the way you read weather.
[It puts itself between you and the sleeping thing it carries, and stays there until you have walked well past. It does not plant anything tonight. It does not trust the ground you stand on.]
